{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Phenytoin\", \"id\": \"D010672\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hepatic injury\", \"id\": \"D056486\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hepatic failure\", \"id\": \"D017093\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"phenytoin\", \"id\": \"D010672\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hepatic injury\", \"id\": \"D056486\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hepatocellular damage\", \"id\": \"D056486\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"drug hypersensitivity\", \"id\": \"D004342\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"phenytoin\", \"id\": \"D010672\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"hepatic injury","id":"D056486","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hepatic failure","id":"D017093","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hepatocellular damage","id":"D056486","label":"Disease"},{"text":"drug hypersensitivity","id":"D004342","label":"Disease"},{"text":"phenytoin","id":"D010672","label":"Chemical"}],"head":"phenytoin","head_id":"D010672","pairs":[{"head":"phenytoin","tail":"hepatic injury","head_id":"D010672","tail_id":"D056486"},{"head":"phenytoin","tail":"hepatic failure","head_id":"D010672","tail_id":"D017093"},{"head":"phenytoin","tail":"drug hypersensitivity","head_id":"D010672","tail_id":"D004342"}],"relations":["D010672 | D056486","D010672 | D017093","D010672 | D004342"],"result":"$","tail":"drug hypersensitivity","tail_id":"D004342","text":"Phenytoin induced fatal hepatic injury. A 61 year old female developed fatal hepatic failure after phenytoin administration. A typical multisystem clinical pattern precedes the manifestations of hepatic injury. The hematologic, biochemical and pathologic features indicate a mixed hepatocellular damage due to drug hypersensitivity. In a patient receiving phenytoin who presents a viral-like illness, early recognition and discontinuation of the drug are mandatory.","metrics":{"precision":0.6666666666666666,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.8,"rel_tp":2,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0}}